WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.633
This lesson explains the safety rules that apply to every website edit.

2
00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:17.136
Make only the approved change, protect the live website, save one time, clear only the applicable cache, verify the exact public result, and stop before a small uncertainty becomes a larger problem.

3
00:00:17.486 --> 00:00:23.317
Use the minimum role assigned to you. Editor is sufficient for routine approved content.

4
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:31.998
Administrator controls, users, plugins, themes, settings, servers, payments, and store integrations require separate authorization.

5
00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:35.907
Never borrow another person's login simply to reach a menu.

6
00:00:36.257 --> 00:00:43.012
Before editing, confirm the live domain, the exact page or record, and the approved replacement information.

7
00:00:43.012 --> 00:00:52.269
If the request is missing a name, date, image, category, link, or final wording, stop before opening the editor and ask for the missing information.

8
00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:59.914
Use rebekahspureliving.com forward slash W P dash admin. Confirm the address begins with the live domain.

9
00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:02.415
Sign in with your own named account.

10
00:01:02.415 --> 00:01:08.321
Do not use an old staging address, a shared account, or another person's saved login.

11
00:01:08.671 --> 00:01:13.760
Choose the correct section, such as Practitioners, Events, Posts, or Pages.

12
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.306
Match the exact title, name, store, and date before selecting Edit.

13
00:01:18.306 --> 00:01:25.702
If two records look similar or the identifying information does not match, stop and confirm the correct item.

14
00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:31.115
Leave unrelated copy, images, categories, links, dates, and settings unchanged.

15
00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:34.767
Do not redesign a page while making a content correction.

16
00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:42.329
Compare the old value with the approved replacement before typing, and reread the complete changed area when finished.

17
00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:47.555
Use Draft for new content until every required detail is complete and approved.

18
00:01:47.555 --> 00:01:52.988
Use Preview to inspect it privately. Do not use Publish merely to see how it might look.

19
00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:58.235
For an existing item, use the approved save action only after the change is reviewed.

20
00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:07.766
Routine editors should not change Appearance, Plugins, Settings, Cloudways, payment, store, integration, or optimization controls.

21
00:02:07.766 --> 00:02:13.062
Do not install, update, disable, reconnect, configure, or restart anything.

22
00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:16.946
Take a screenshot of the problem and contact Blue Nova.

23
00:02:17.296 --> 00:02:22.691
Confirm images are approved and correctly cropped. Open every changed link.

24
00:02:22.691 --> 00:02:29.955
Recheck dates, times, prices, health wording, addresses, phone numbers, names, and store information.

25
00:02:29.955 --> 00:02:35.278
These details can cause customer confusion when a small typo is published.

26
00:02:35.628 --> 00:02:39.509
Choose Save, Update, or Publish according to the approved task.

27
00:02:39.509 --> 00:02:43.883
Select the correct button one time and wait for WordPress confirmation.

28
00:02:43.883 --> 00:02:50.659
Do not click repeatedly, close the page while it is saving, or create a duplicate item to work around a delay.

29
00:02:51.009 --> 00:02:58.436
Start with the exact record or page cache when available. Use broader Breeze or Varnish purges only when approved.

30
00:02:58.436 --> 00:03:05.341
Do not clear unrelated caches and do not change plugin, cache, server, database, or optimization settings.

31
00:03:05.691 --> 00:03:09.737
Open the exact canonical public address with no extra text.

32
00:03:09.737 --> 00:03:15.291
Confirm the visible change and test affected controls at desktop and phone sizes.

33
00:03:15.291 --> 00:03:20.777
If the result is wrong, missing, or broken, stop. Do not keep saving or purging.

34
00:03:20.777 --> 00:03:23.657
Record what you see and contact Blue Nova.

35
00:03:24.007 --> 00:03:33.511
Safe editing means opening the correct item, making only the approved change, saving once, clearing only the applicable cache, and verifying publicly.

36
00:03:33.511 --> 00:03:41.113
Stop whenever the task, screen, permission, save result, or public page does not match what these instructions describe.
